{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-001","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Opening — awareness and Father","quote_original":"You can say I AM not that, but you cannot say I AM not, for your very knowing is a declaration that you are.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["i-am","awareness","being"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-002","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Opening — awareness and Father","quote_original":"You are spiritually distilled or extracted from your conception of yourself when you cease to be identified with it.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["self-concept","identity","non-attachment"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-003","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"I Come With a Sword — self-concept","quote_original":"Your present attachments are rooted in you because of your present conception of yourself. Your conception of yourself is the measuring rod by which you measure the world.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["self-concept","attachments","perception"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-004","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"I Come With a Sword — self-concept","quote_original":"Change your conception of yourself. Revalue yourself and you will automatically change your world.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["self-concept","change","world"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-005","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Foundation Stone — consciousness and feeling","quote_original":"Awareness of being precedes all conceptions of itself and remains its formless self when all of its conceptions cease to be. The creator must precede creation, as the conceiver precedes his conceptions.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["awareness","conception","creation"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-006","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Foundation Stone — consciousness and feeling","quote_original":"To change the expression change the conception of yourself but do so in truth, not in words.","primary_topic":"SELF_CONCEPT","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["self-concept","change","conviction"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-007","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Foundation Stone — consciousness and feeling","quote_original":"Ask yourself this simple question. How would I feel if I were free?","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","freedom","self-questioning"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-008","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Foundation Stone — consciousness and feeling","quote_original":"Make the new feeling natural by wearing it. All things express their nature, so you must wear this feeling until it becomes your nature.","primary_topic":"FEELING","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["feeling","naturalness","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-009","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"The I’m-pression","quote_original":"To say that I shall be great or that I shall be free is a confession that I am not great and I Am not free. To see yourself as becoming anything is to know that I am not that thing.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["present-tense","assumption","identity"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-010","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"The I’m-pression","quote_original":"Let all your desires be impressions of that which is, not that which is to be.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["FEELING"],"tags":["desire","impression","present-tense"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-011","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"The I’m-pression","quote_original":"Signs follow, they do not precede.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["signs","assumption","sequence"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-012","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"The I’m-pression","quote_original":"You cannot express that which you are not conscious of being. You cannot serve two masters. Your master is ever that state of consciousness with which you are identified.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["SELF_CONCEPT"],"tags":["state","identity","consciousness"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-013","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Crucifixion and Resurrection","quote_original":"Your awareness images and out-pictures all that you are aware of being.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["REALITY_CIRCUMSTANCES"],"tags":["awareness","out-picturing","state"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-014","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Will and present-tense fulfillment","quote_original":"When a sculptor looks at a formless piece of marble he sees buried within its formless self, his finished piece of art. So the sculptor instead of making his masterpiece, merely reveals it, by removing that part of the marble which hides his conception.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["IMAGINATION"],"tags":["sculptor","finished-state","conception"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-015","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"The Door / senses","quote_original":"There is only one door through which That Which You Seek can enter your world. When you say, I AM, you are declaring yourself to be first person, present tense.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["i-am","present-tense","desire"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-016","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Closing — expression and appearance","quote_original":"Your awareness never asks permission to express that which you are aware of being.","primary_topic":"CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM","secondary_topics":["ASSUMPTION"],"tags":["awareness","expression","assumption"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
{"quote_id":"IKMF-CUR-017","corpus_id":"B013","author":"Neville Goddard","source_title":"I Know My Father","source_year":1960,"source_slug":"i_know_my_father","source_section":"Closing — expression and appearance","quote_original":"BE CONSCIOUS OF BEING THAT WHICH YOU WANT TO APPEAR.","primary_topic":"ASSUMPTION","secondary_topics":["CONSCIOUSNESS_I_AM"],"tags":["being","appearance","assumption"],"editorial_decision":"SELECT","review_mode":"SOURCE_FIRST_CANONICAL","source_file":"master_text_i_know_my_father.txt","review_policy":"EDITORIAL_POLICY.md"}
